{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_constitution_amendments_amendment_log", "label": "Constitution Amendment Log", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/CONSTITUTION-AMENDMENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Append-only; every entry follows Article XXV's five-part format and each adopted entry is also recorded as an AMEND_CONSTITUTION contribution carrying the new constitution_hash."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_constitution_amendments_adoption_1_0_0", "label": "Amendment 1.0.0 \u2014 Initial Adoption", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/CONSTITUTION-AMENDMENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Articles I\u2013XXV adopted as written; only editorial additions (precedence header, shall/should definitions, scope, and the rule requiring Constitutional Test answers to be recorded for sensitive features)."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_constitution_amendments_p_1", "label": "P-1 \u2014 Protection of Persons", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/CONSTITUTION-AMENDMENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A permanent, signed, append-only ledger of scored assertions is an unusually durable defamation and doxxing vector; the constitution protects contributors' privacy but says nothing about the people claims are about. The safeguard against abusing the restriction power is that restriction is never silent."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_constitution_amendments_p_2", "label": "P-2 \u2014 Lawful Removal Is Visible", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/CONSTITUTION-AMENDMENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Article XIII forbids erasing contributions merely for being wrong, which does not address legally compelled removal. A visible tombstone can leak that something sensitive existed; accepted as the lesser harm compared with silent removal. Implemented as the TAKEDOWN action."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_constitution_amendments_p_3", "label": "P-3 \u2014 Designations of \"Unknowable\" Are Themselves Claims", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/CONSTITUTION-AMENDMENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Without this, labeling a claim untestable could shield it from evidence \u2014 the evidence-free denial Article XXIII warns against, pointed the other way."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_constitution_amendments_p_4", "label": "P-4 \u2014 Strength of Evidence for Extraordinary Conclusions", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/CONSTITUTION-AMENDMENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Posed as a question, not text: an auditable prior_class would hand whoever sets it real power over outcomes, so the spec takes option (a), accepting flat priors as a v0.1 limitation."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_constitution_amendments_p_5", "label": "P-5 \u2014 The Ledger Runs No Model", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/CONSTITUTION-AMENDMENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A model running inside the ledger would be an unattributed, unreproducible contributor whose outputs could not be replayed, audited or challenged. Keeping every model outside, behind a signed contribution, is what makes 'reproducible from the log' true."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_constitution_amendments_p_6", "label": "P-6 \u2014 Money Buys No Part of the Record", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/CONSTITUTION-AMENDMENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Article XII names commercial capture but says nothing about the money that keeps a node running. The harm here is not a rewritten entry, which the log would expose, but an unrecorded arrangement that never touches the log at all; naming every sponsor applies Article XII's rule against silence to funding."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_constitution_amendments_p_1", "target": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_article_xii", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/CONSTITUTION-AMENDMENTS.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_constitution_amendments_amendment_log", "target": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_constitution_amendments_p_1", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/CONSTITUTION-AMENDMENTS.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_constitution_amendments_p_2", "target": "d